      "id": "AspNet.AssetManager",
      "range": "*"
    },
    "message": "Renamed twice: to AspNetWebpack in v1.0.0, then to AspNet.AssetManager in v3.0.0. Install AspNet.AssetManager instead. It supports Webpack and Vite and targets .NET 8, 9 and 10. Each rename changed the package ID, the namespace and the services.Add...() method, and v4.0.0 renamed the Webpack configuration section to AssetManager. The release notes for v1.0.0, v3.0.0 and v4.0.0 list every breaking change: https://github.com/Baune8D/AspNet.AssetManager/releases",
    "reasons": [
      "Legacy"
    ]
  },
